    {
      "id": "6abbeb168ea2-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "If \\({\\left( {\\sqrt 5 } \\right)^5} \\times {25^2} = {5^x} \\times 5\\sqrt 5,\\) then x is equal to",
      "questionHtml": "<p>If <span class=\"math-tex\">\\({\\left( {\\sqrt 5 } \\right)^5} \\times {25^2} = {5^x} \\times 5\\sqrt 5,\\)</span>&nbsp;then x is equal to</p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "2",
          "html": "2"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "3",
          "html": "3"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "4",
          "html": "4"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "5",
          "html": "5"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>To solve questions of this type, follow the laws of &ldquo;Surds and indices&rsquo;&rsquo; given below-</p>\n\n<p><strong>Laws of Indices:-</strong></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\begin{array}{l} 1 - :\\;{a^m} \\times {a^n} = {a^{\\left\\{ {m + n} \\right\\}}}\\\\ 2 - :\\;{a^m} \\div {a^n} = {a^{\\left\\{ {m - n} \\right\\}}}\\\\ 3 - :\\;{\\left( {{a^m}} \\right)^n} = {a^{mn}}\\\\ 4 - :{\\left( a \\right)^{ - m}} = \\frac{1}{{{a^m}}}\\\\ 5 - :{\\left( a \\right)^{\\frac{m}{n}}} = \\sqrt[n]{{{a^m}}}\\\\ 6 - :{\\left( a \\right)^0} = 1 \\end{array}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>Given,</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\begin{array}{l} {\\left( {\\sqrt 5 } \\right)^5} \\times {25^2} = {5^x} \\times 5\\sqrt 5 \\\\ \\Rightarrow {5^{\\frac{5}{2}}} \\times {5^4} = {5^x} \\times 5 \\times {5^{\\frac{1}{2}}} \\end{array}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 5<sup>13/2 </sup>= 5<sup>x + 3/2 </sup></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 13/2 = x + 3/2</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; x = 5</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
